.TH AMAYA 1 "October 2026" "Amaya 11.4.7+modern1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
amaya \- WYSIWYG editor and browser for structured web pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amaya
.RI [ file | URL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Amaya
edits web pages as they look: text is typed, selected and restyled on the
formatted page, while Amaya keeps a clean, valid document structure
underneath (XHTML, HTML\ 4, CSS, MathML, SVG).  Structure, source, links
and table-of-contents views are kept in step with the formatted view.
Amaya is also a simple web browser (http and https, forms, cookies), without
JavaScript.
.PP
Without an argument, Amaya opens its welcome page.  With a file name or an
http/https address, it opens that document.
.PP
The user manual is in the program: \fBHelp > Amaya Help\fR (F1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.amaya/
Per-user files: \fIthot.rc\fR (preferences), \fIamaya.keyboard\fR (personal
shortcuts, replacing the installed ones), \fIcookies.txt\fR,
\fItrusted-certs.pem\fR (certificates trusted in addition to the system's).
.TP
.I /usr/share/amaya/
Installed data: configuration, keyboard shortcuts, menu texts, schemas,
icons, fonts, dictionaries and the user manual.
.TP
.I /usr/share/amaya/contrib/firefox-cookies.py
Copies the cookies of one site from Firefox, for \fBFile > Load cookies\fR.
The resulting file holds login credentials: delete it after use.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMAYA_USER_HOME
Directory used instead of \fI~/.amaya\fR, if it exists.
.TP
.BR http_proxy ", " https_proxy
Proxy for web access (the proxy preference is not used).
